## ⚡ Performance & Database

**N+1 Query Detection in PRs** — Identifies unoptimized eager loading in loops and recommends `->with()` or `->load()` refinements during code inspection.
- **Use when:** Reviewing database-heavy features, list endpoints, or API resource collections.
- **Example:** `❌ foreach ($posts as $post) { echo $post->author->name; }` → `✅ $posts = Post::with('author')->get();`
- **Source:** https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/eloquent-loading

**Eloquent Query Builder Optimization** — Recommends raw queries, chunking, or `cursor()` when ORM abstractions introduce memory leaks or unnecessary overhead.
- **Use when:** Reviewing complex aggregations, background export jobs, or large-scale data migrations.
- **Source:** https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/queries

**Database Index & Migration Review** — Validates that foreign keys, frequently filtered columns, and composite search paths have corresponding indexes. Flags missing `unsigned()` or `nullable()` constraints.
- **Use when:** Reviewing new migrations, schema changes, or slow-query reports.
- **Source:** https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/migrations

**Caching Strategy & Invalidation Audit** — Ensures cache tags are used for grouped invalidation, TTLs match data volatility, and race conditions (stale reads) are prevented via atomic cache-and-update patterns.
- **Use when:** Reviewing read-heavy endpoints, session handlers, or computed dashboard metrics.
- **Source:** https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/cache

**Performance Profiling & Regression Detection** — Flags new unbounded loops, missing indexes, or synchronous heavy computations introduced in diffs. Recommends Blackfire/Tideways integration for baseline comparison.
- **Use when:** Reviewing optimization PRs, auditing feature additions, or monitoring SLO deviations.
- **Source:** https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/optimization

