## 🧪 Testing & Validation

**Validation & Form Request Compliance** — Ensures input rules are centralized in dedicated Form Requests. Enforces role-based validation logic and reusable rule sets.
- **Use when:** Reviewing POST/PUT endpoints, auditing data integrity, or enforcing DRY validation.
- **Source:** https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/validation#form-request-validation

**Test Coverage & Assertion Validation** — Checks for meaningful assertions, proper test isolation (`RefreshDatabase`), and missing edge-case coverage. Flags brittle UI tests or over-mocked unit tests.
- **Use when:** Reviewing feature branches, validating bug fixes, or checking test coverage.
- **Source:** https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/testing

**Testing Strategy & Mock Boundaries** — Validates appropriate use of `Mockery`/`PHPUnit` stubs vs. real repository/database layers. Enforces TDD/BDD patterns where applicable.
- **Use when:** Reviewing unit test suites, refactoring legacy test code, or establishing team testing standards.
- **Source:** https://phpunit.readthedocs.io/en/11.0/test-doubles.html

