## 🛠 CI/CD, Static Analysis & Governance

**Laravel Pint Interpretation** — Translates Pint warnings into actionable formatting steps. PHPStan/Larastan are not installed; do not treat them as available unless added to the project.
- **Use when:** Reviewing Pint output or fixing formatting issues.
- **Source:** https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/pint

**Branch Protection & PR Governance** — Enforces required status checks, minimum reviewers, conventional commits, and linear history. Prevents force pushes to protected branches.
- **Use when:** Configuring repository settings, establishing team PR policies, or auditing CI/CD pipelines.
- **Source:** https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/configuring-branches-and-merges-in-your-repository/defining-the-mergeability-of-pull-requests/about-protected-branches

**Documentation & Contract Compliance** — Validates inline docblocks, API resource schemas, OpenAPI/Swagger specs, and external developer guides. Ensures public APIs are versioned and backward-compatible.
- **Use when:** Reviewing public APIs, preparing releases, or maintaining team knowledge bases.
- **Source:** https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/requests

